nning thugs for ancient  artifacts finally they settled on a  prequel to uncharted drake's Fortune  titled  uncharted golden Abyss wherein nate is  hired by his old friend jason dante to  uncover secrets and treasures in the  Central American jungle utilizing some  of the Vedas unique functionality  players were able to take charcoal  rubbings using the front touch screen  uncover hidden messages by holding their  system up to a bright light and aim  weapons and the in-game SLR camera using  the Vita's gyro the game launched  alongside the Vita in 2011 and went on  to sell 1.7 million copies worldwide it  proved that triple-a game experiences  usually associated with home consoles  were capable on a portable system at the  conclusion of their time with uncharted  Sony Ben went dark rumors swirled online  as to what they were working on in 2014  a leak purported to show concept art  from a work-in-progress open-world  horror game some of the art showed  characters wearing a very familiar white  and black headset the Ben logo fades  under the screen at Sony's e3 conference  days gone kicks off the conference's  trailer block with an affecting human  look at its tortured protagonists and  post-apocalyptic world before closing  out Sony's conference with a six minute  gameplay presentation highlighting the  impressive freak awards and  environmental gameplay after five years  of silence bender back and from the  looks of it they're coming back bigger  than they've ever been before so that's  a brief --is-- history of Sony Bend  have you checked out any of their games  over the years and what do you think of  what we've seen up days gone make sure  to let us know in the comments and for  more on Days gone keep it parked at  GameSpot
 

